#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:3
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr "Najczęściej zadawane pytania"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:10
msgid "Why not just wrap at 80 columns?"
msgstr "Dlaczego nie zawijać po prostu przy 80 kolumnach?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:12
msgid ""
"Column wrapping causes paragraph-wide reflows when you change a single word. "
"Reviewers see the entire paragraph in the diff, obscuring the actual edit. "
"Sentence-per-line formatting means a one-word change produces a one-line "
"diff."
msgstr ""
"Zawijanie kolumnowe powoduje przepływ całego akapitu przy zmianie jednego "
"słowa. Recenzenci widzą cały akapit w diff-ie, co zasłania rzeczywistą "
"zmianę. Formatowanie jedno-zdanie-na-linię sprawia, że zmiana jednego słowa "
"daje jednolinijkowy diff."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:19
msgid "Does this affect how the document renders?"
msgstr "Czy wpływa to na wygląd wyrenderowanego dokumentu?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:21
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"No. LaTeX, Org-mode, Markdown, RST, and most prose formats treat single "
"newlines as whitespace. Two consecutive newlines start a new paragraph. "
"Snapper preserves paragraph breaks (blank lines) and only changes where "
"single newlines occur within a paragraph."
msgstr ""
"Nie. LaTeX, Org-mode, Markdown i większość formatów tekstowych traktuje "
"pojedyncze znaki nowej linii jako spacje. Dwa kolejne znaki nowej linii "
"rozpoczynają nowy akapit. Snapper zachowuje podziały akapitów (puste linie) "
"i zmienia tylko miejsca, gdzie pojedyncze znaki nowej linii występują "
"wewnątrz akapitu."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:26
msgid "My collaborators don't use snapper."
msgstr "Moi współpracownicy nie używają snappera."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:28
msgid "Will this cause problems?"
msgstr "Czy to spowoduje problemy?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:30
msgid ":CUSTOM\\ :sub:`ID`\\: collaborators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:32
msgid ""
"No. The formatting affects only whitespace within paragraphs. Collaborators "
"can edit normally and their changes will merge cleanly. For fully "
"transparent integration, use a git smudge/clean filter (see the how-to "
"guide)."
msgstr ""
"Nie. Formatowanie wpływa tylko na białe znaki wewnątrz akapitów. "
"Współpracownicy mogą edytować normalnie, a ich zmiany będą się łączyć bez "
"konfliktów. Dla w pełni przezroczystej integracji użyj filtra git smudge/"
"clean (zobacz przewodnik)."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:39
#, fuzzy
msgid "Why does snapper handle \"Dr. Smith\" correctly?"
msgstr "Dlaczego snapper dzieli \"Dr."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:41
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Snapper maintains curated abbreviation lists for English (80+), German, "
"French, Icelandic, and Polish. After Unicode sentence boundary detection, it "
"merges any splits that occurred at known abbreviation periods. Select a "
"language with ``--lang de`` (or set ``lang = \"de\"`` in "
"``.snapperrc.toml``). You can also add project-specific abbreviations via "
"``extra_abbreviations`` in the config file."
msgstr ""
"Snapper utrzymuje starannie dobraną listę ponad 80 skrótów (tytuły, terminy "
"łacińskie, odniesienia naukowe, jednoliterowe inicjały). Po wykryciu granic "
"zdań Unicode łączy podziały, które wystąpiły przy znanych kropkach skrótów. "
"Możesz dodać skróty specyficzne dla projektu w ``.snapperrc.toml``."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:49
msgid "What about non-English text?"
msgstr "Co z tekstem w językach innych niż angielski?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:51
msgid "Snapper supports non-English text in two ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:53
msgid ""
"**Rule-based abbreviation sets** for German (``de``), French (``fr``), "
"Icelandic (``is``), and Polish (``pl``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:55
msgid ""
"Select with ``--lang de``. The Unicode UAX #29 sentence boundary algorithm "
"works across all languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:58
msgid ""
"**Neural sentence detection** via nnsplit for 9 languages (en, de, fr, no, "
"sv, zh, tr, ru, uk)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:60
msgid ""
"Enable with ``--neural --lang de``. Models download on first use (~4MB, "
"cached)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:63
msgid ""
"The rule-based approach handles most academic text well and runs 18x faster. "
"Use neural for languages where abbreviation rules fall short (Chinese, "
"Turkish, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:69
#, fuzzy
msgid "Why does ``snapper`` conflict with openSUSE?"
msgstr "Dlaczego snapper dzieli \"Dr."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:71
msgid ""
"`openSUSE snapper <https://github.com/openSUSE/snapper>`_ is a different "
"project (Btrfs/LVM volume snapshots) that also installs a ``snapper`` "
"binary. This formatter's crate name is ``snapper-fmt``; installers ship both "
"``snapper`` and ``snapper-fmt`` as names for the same program. On systems "
"where openSUSE already owns ``/usr/bin/snapper``, invoke ``snapper-fmt`` (or "
"put the TurtleTech install directory first on ``PATH``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:78
msgid "Can I use snapper as a library?"
msgstr "Czy mogę używać snappera jako biblioteki?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:80
msgid ""
"Yes. The crate (``snapper-fmt``) exposes ``format_text()`` and all internal "
"modules:"
msgstr ""
"Tak. Crate (``snapper-fmt``) udostępnia ``format_text()`` i wszystkie "
"wewnętrzne moduły:"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:101
msgid "How fast is it?"
msgstr "Jak szybki jest snapper?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:103
msgid ""
"Snapper processes typical academic papers (10-50 pages) in under 10ms with "
"the rule-based splitter. Neural mode adds ~200ms per file (model load + "
"inference via tract, pure Rust ONNX). No external runtime dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:110
msgid "What about CRLF line endings?"
msgstr "Co ze znakami końca linii CRLF?"

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:112
msgid ""
"Snapper detects the input's line ending convention (LF or CRLF) and "
"preserves it in the output. Internally, processing normalizes to LF and "
"converts back before writing."
msgstr ""
"Snapper wykrywa konwencję znaków końca linii wejścia (LF lub CRLF) i "
"zachowuje ją na wyjściu. Wewnętrznie przetwarzanie normalizuje do LF i "
"konwertuje z powrotem przed zapisem."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:118
msgid "Can I skip formatting for specific sections?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:120
msgid "Yes. Use ``snapper:off`` and ``snapper:on`` pragmas in comments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:123
msgid "Org: ``# snapper:off`` / ``# snapper:on``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:125
msgid ""
"LaTeX: ``% snapper:off`` / ``% snapper:on``; ``% snapper:no-preamble`` on "
"``\\input`` chapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:127
msgid "Markdown: ``<!-- snapper:off -->`` / ``<!-- snapper:on -->``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:129
msgid "RST/Plaintext: ``snapper:off`` / ``snapper:on`` on their own line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:131
msgid ""
"Text between these markers passes through unchanged. Useful for poetry, "
"aligned text, or ASCII art."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:137
#, fuzzy
msgid "What formats does snapper support?"
msgstr "Dlaczego snapper dzieli \"Dr."

#: ../../source/faq/index.rst:139
msgid ""
"Org-mode, LaTeX, Markdown, reStructuredText, and plaintext. Format auto-"
"detects from the file extension (``.org``, ``.tex``, ``.md``, ``.rst``, "
"``.txt``). Unknown extensions (``.rs``, ``.py``, no extension) are refused "
"so source files are not treated as prose. Override with ``--format rst`` (or "
"``org``, ``latex``, ``markdown``, ``plaintext``)."
msgstr ""

